{"kind":"artifact","text":"The cloned-repo how-to stops telling a reader the two surfaces disagree, because at this head they do not. Exact clean pushed head 128132f23c3ea13e7b0ed93e33735f6181531c92; tree unchanged from 9d3e6483, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's child 467ad483 and my promise 5ee01d7b.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, at the tamper walkthrough around line 447. The page followed its worked tampering example with a paragraph saying the MCP adapter decides this differently and treats an untrustworthy record as no resident, because a long-lived session has no per-call way to refuse an attachment. The premise was the defect: there is a per-call way, the adapter now uses it, and the paragraph now says so. A durable call through the adapter stops with the same reason, a read still answers from the verified local fold, and it refuses the call rather than the attachment — so a long-lived session survives a record it can repair, and deleting the record is the whole recovery there too.\n\nWHY THIS PAGE PARTICULARLY. It is where somebody actually tampers with a record and watches what happens. A reader who does that here and then reads that the other surface would have shrugged learns something false about the system's safety, in the one place they were most likely to trust it. That is worse than the same sentence sitting in a reference page, which is why this correction belongs in the same head as the fix rather than in a later documentation pass.\n\nThe surrounding executable walkthrough is unchanged; only the paragraph interpreting it moved.\n\nGATES, from runs I watched exit at this exact head. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 35 packages, 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached — internal/docset uncached at 172.454s, cmd/gs 318.689s, cmd/gitseq-mcp 206.823s. npm test 87 pass, 0 fail after npm ci in this worktree; the first run failed five files on a missing node_modules, which was the worktree and not this change. gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"128132f23c3ea13e7b0ed93e33735f6181531c92","path":"docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md"}}